
If you want these scripts to run on a schedule, you don’t need anything complicated. On macOS or Linux, crontab -e handles it:


# Run uptime check every 5 minutes
*/5 * * * * /usr/bin/python3 /home/user/scripts/uptime_monitor.py

# Weekly email report, Monday at 7 AM
0 7 * * 1 /usr/bin/python3 /home/user/scripts/email_report.py

# Git backup every Sunday at midnight
0 0 * * 0 /usr/bin/python3 /home/user/scripts/git_backup.py
